            <div xml:id="d145">

                <pb facs="0230" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 551/87–88.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador O’Brien to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-01-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 171.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a dispatch from the consul at Dalny, in which it is stated that the Port
                    Arthur branch of the Imperial Chinese Maritime Customs at Dairen was finally
                    opened on the 8th instant, and stating that the rumors to the effect that Port
                    Arthur was to be opened to foreign trade on the same basis as Dairen has now
                    been officially denied.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. J. O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d145-a1.xml" xpointer="d145-a1"/>
            </div>
